Here is the **simplest exam-ready C program** that satisfies *exactly* those rules. No extra complications.

---

## ✅ **VALIDATION RULES**
- **At least 1 lowercase** letter `[a-z]`  
- **At least 1 digit** `[0-9]`  
- **At least 1 uppercase** letter `[A-Z]`  
- **At least 1 special** from **{ $, #, @ }**  
- **Length between 6 and 12**

---

## ✅ **SIMPLE C PROGRAM (Beginner-friendly)**

```c
#include <stdio.h>
#include <string.h>
#include <ctype.h>

int main() {
    char pw[50];
    int i, len;
    int lower = 0, upper = 0, digit = 0, special = 0;

    printf("Enter password: ");
    scanf("%s", pw);

    len = strlen(pw);

    // length check
    if (len < 6 || len > 12) {
        printf("Invalid\n");
        return 0;
    }

    // check each character
    for (i = 0; i < len; i++) {
        if (islower(pw[i]))
            lower = 1;
        else if (isupper(pw[i]))
            upper = 1;
        else if (isdigit(pw[i]))
            digit = 1;
        else if (pw[i] == '$' || pw[i] == '#' || pw[i] == '@')
            special = 1;
    }

    // final validation
    if (lower && upper && digit && special)
        printf("Valid\n");
    else
        printf("Invalid\n");

    return 0;
}
```

---

## ✅ **HOW IT WORKS (Ultra-simple explanation)**

- `islower()` → checks small letters  
- `isupper()` → checks capital letters  
- `isdigit()` → checks numbers  
- Loop checks if each condition is found at least once  
- Finally prints **Valid** only if all flags are **1**

